              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "धागा (dhāgā) is a tadbhava, a word inherited and reshaped by sound change. It comes from dhāgga, \"thread\", a form CDIAL reconstructs from its descendants (CDIAL 6770). Where dhāgga came from is not settled: CDIAL says it was possibly crossed with dhara, \"a flock of raw cotton\", but points as well to a second thread-word, trāgga."
